abstract: >-
  batlab is a Python research library for lithium-ion battery degradation
  analysis: standardized dataset loaders (NASA PCoE, Severson 2019, Oxford
  Path-Dependent 2020, CALCE CS2), literature-cited feature engineering,
  leave-cell-out-validated GBRT SOH/RUL models, and reproducible benchmark
  manifests. Built around the position that a battery-ML result is only
  useful if it is validated honestly (leave-cell-out, not a row-level
  split) and reported with its actual sample size and reliability, not
  just a headline R-squared.
